{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-harness-seam-018-01", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/TestCommandTimeJumpTests.cs", "line": 262, "method": "CompletePayload_FractionalDelta_NoLocaleComma", "category": "T3", "severity": "Low", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/TestCommands/TestCommandTimeJump.cs:167; drop CultureInfo.InvariantCulture from the delta ToString -> red on a ro-RO / de-DE host, still green on the en-US or invariant host CI runs", "what_it_asserts": "That BuildPayload's delta for a 0.5 s jump renders as \"0.5\" with no comma.", "why_weak": "It never forces a culture, so on CI (and any dot-decimal host) it passes against a CurrentCulture-formatted site; the guard only bites on the maintainer's own machine. The sibling cell at line 252 asserts integers only, which no culture changes, so nothing in this file pins the invariance on CI.", "proposed_action": "Wrap the assertion in the CultureSwap(\"de-DE\") helper already used in TestCommandCaptureScreenshotTests / TestCommandDumpGuiTreeTests, so the fractional delta proves the production site is invariant rather than that the host is.", "effort": "S", "july_ref": "none"}
